      "text": "Read left to right: the big board is the whole idea, the three small ones are the states, and the last is what happens after a run.\n\nNothing here is wired. The selection IS the input set."
    },
    {
      "id": "q-head",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 760,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "The output node held three things: what to make, from what, and with which settings — and it held them BETWEEN runs. Selection replaces the first two. These are three answers to the third.\n\nThey are not exclusive: A is the floor, B and C are things you can add on top of it."
    },
